{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_0112r2wrw7qttqw2jxUgbHUx","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"## Project State Summary\n\n**Problem**: GNU coreutils lack formal specs accessible to implementers. This project derives specs from C source, generates Go implementations via AI, and verifies parity via differential testing against Homebrew GNU binaries.\n\n**Architecture**: Four-stage pipeline (extract → specify → synthesize → verify). `cmd/` holds one utility per directory, `pkg/testutils` provides the differential testing harness, `pkg/sys` wraps syscalls, `pkg/format` handles output formatting. Mage targets drive the orchestrator.\n\n**Current state**: This is generation run 44 on a specs-only repo. Several utilities are already implemented in this run (sponge, du, true, false, yes, basename, dirname, tee, plus pkg/ infrastructure). cmd/head has R1.1-R1.4 completed per the latest commit.\n\n**Current release**: rel02.2 (head + seq). head has 13 remaining ready requirements (R1.5, R2.1-R2.3, R3.1-R3.5, R4.1-R4.4). seq has 17 ready requirements.\n\n## Priority Analysis\n\nThe earliest incomplete work is **srd018-head** in rel02.2, with 13 ready requirements remaining. All 4 task slots should go to finishing head, since seq can follow in the next batch.\n\n## Weight Budget Check\n\nAll srd018-head requirements assumed weight=1 (default):\n\n- Task 0: R1.5(1) + R2.1(1) + R2.2(1) + R2.3(1) = 4 ✓\n- Task 1: R3.1(1) + R3.2(1) + R3.3(1) + R3.4(1) = 4 ✓\n- Task 2: R3.5(1) + R4.1(1) + R4.2(1) + R4.3(1) = 4 ✓\n- Task 3: R4.4(1) = 1 ✓\n\n```yaml\n- index: 0\n  title: \"[stitch] cmd/head: byte-count mode and remaining core behavior (srd018-head R1.5, R2.1-R2.3)\"\n  dependency: -1\n  description: |\n    deliverable_type: code\n\n    required_reading:\n      - docs/specs/software-requirements/srd018-head.yaml (SRD for head -- focus on R1.5, R2.1, R2.2, R2.3)\n      - cmd/head/main.go (existing implementation covering R1.1-R1.4: basic line output and defaults)\n      - cmd/head/head_test.go (existing differential tests for R1.1-R1.4)\n      - pkg/testutils/ (DiffTest struct and RunDiffTests for differential testing)\n      - pkg/sys/ (InstallSIGPIPEHandler, already called in main)\n\n    files:\n      - path: cmd/head/main.go\n        action: modify\n        note: \"Add byte-count mode, negative count support, and remaining group-1/group-2 behavior\"\n      - path: cmd/head/head_test.go\n        action: modify\n        note: \"Add differential test cases for R1.5, R2.1, R2.2, R2.3 using ghead as reference\"\n\n    requirements:\n      - id: R1\n        text: \"Implement srd018-head R1.5 per the SRD specification\"\n      - id: R2\n        text: \"Implement srd018-head R2.1 per the SRD specification\"\n      - id: R3\n        text: \"Implement srd018-head R2.2 per the SRD specification\"\n      - id: R4\n        text: \"Implement srd018-head R2.3 per the SRD specification\"\n\n    design_decisions:\n      - id: D1\n        text: \"Extend the existing flag-parsing and output logic established by R1.1-R1.4 in main.go\"\n      - id: D2\n        text: \"Use pkg/testutils.RunDiffTests with ghead as the reference binary for all new test cases\"\n      - id: D3\n        text: \"Set LC_ALL=C in test environment per project convention\"\n\n    acceptance_criteria:\n      - id: AC1\n        text: \"go build ./cmd/head/ succeeds with no errors\"\n      - id: AC2\n        text: \"go vet ./cmd/head/ reports no issues\"\n      - id: AC3\n        text: \"go test ./cmd/head/... -count=1 passes (or skips gracefully if ghead not in PATH)\"\n      - id: AC4\n        text: \"Requirements R1.5, R2.1, R2.2, R2.3 are implemented in main.go with corresponding differential tests\"\n\n- index: 1\n  title: \"[stitch] cmd/head: multi-file headers and quiet/verbose control (srd018-head R3.1-R3.4)\"\n  dependency: 0\n  description: |\n    deliverable_type: code\n\n    required_reading:\n      - docs/specs/s